  "observations": [
    "All 24 retained originals were individually viewed at original resolution. Light and dark settings show complete select menus, checked and unchecked switches, red invalid-field borders and complete blue close-button keyboard outlines.",
    "The narrow and zoomed settings views retain the close action and independent sidebar/body scrollbars. Lower categories and keyboard-shortcut rows require vertical scrolling; the connection form image shows its bottom save action after scrolling.",
    "Disabled tray-dependent controls have faint text and switch tracks. The screenshots establish the captured visual state, not physical assistive-technology usability or contrast compliance.",
    "Close, edge-positioned and disabled-button hints are visible. The long literal HTML-like title wraps in the tooltip without rendering markup; the title itself remains truncated.",
    "Light and dark startup fallback images show the centered independent Nook mark. Both wide and narrow recovery-error views retain the full message and reload action. These are isolated startup fixtures, not corrupt-vault recovery."
  ],
